  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.55 Nameplate capacity",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.55 “Nameplate capacity” means the maximum electrical output, in MWe, that a generator can sustain over a specified period of time when not restricted by seasonal or other deratings as measured in accordance with the U.S. Department of Energy standards.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09 (from Env-A 4602.56); ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.56); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.56)",
